# Third party assets

The code in this repository is MIT licensed. See LICENSE.

The exercise illustrations under `web/public/exercises/` are **not** covered by that license. They
are third party works licensed under CC BY-SA, credited individually in `web/ATTRIBUTIONS.md`, and
they remain under their own license and its share-alike terms.

This note lives here rather than at the end of LICENSE on purpose. GitHub detects a repository's
license by matching the file against the known license texts, and any paragraph appended after the
MIT body makes the match fail: the repository then reports `NOASSERTION` instead of `MIT`, which is
what several directory listings read when they score a project.
